            <fr:title text="Incorrect Specifications">Incorrect Specifications</fr:title>
            <fr:meta name="toc">true</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
    Incorrect software specifications are a problem because
    they can invalidate the security guarantees offered by <fr:link href="/dhsorens-000X/" title="Formal Specification and Verification" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-000X/" display-uri="dhsorens-000X" type="local">formal verification</fr:link>, 
    offer a false sense of security,
    misguide developers,
    and most importantly open code up to vulnerabilities.
    Indeed, for <fr:link href="/dhsorens-000Y/" title="Smart Contracts" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-000Y/" display-uri="dhsorens-000Y" type="local">smart contracts</fr:link>, poor specifications are a <fr:link href="/dhsorens-001P/" title="Smart Contract Vulnerabilities Due to Poor Specification" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-001P/" display-uri="dhsorens-001P" type="local">common source of catastrophic vulnerabilities and losses of funds</fr:link>.
</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
