            <fr:title text="Summary of Work and Projects">Summary of Work and Projects</fr:title>
            <fr:meta name="toc">true</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
    Since early 2018 I have held various roles in crypto, working mostly in research and <fr:link href="/dhsorens-000X/" title="Formal Specification and Verification" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-000X/" display-uri="dhsorens-000X" type="local">formal verification</fr:link>.
    My original interests in crypto were in consensus algorithms and formal verification frameworks for verifying smart contracts. When I started, those frameworks and tools were in their infancy, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-001D/" title="The K Framework" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-001D/" display-uri="dhsorens-001D" type="local">K Framework</fr:link> being the only tool at the time to my knowledge that was production-ready for actual smart contracts.

    Over time, I became interested in the financial applications of <fr:link href="/dhsorens-000Y/" title="Smart Contracts" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-000Y/" display-uri="dhsorens-000Y" type="local">smart contracts</fr:link> and I did my <fr:link href="/dhsorens-phd/" title="PhD in Formal Methods" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-phd/" display-uri="dhsorens-phd" type="local">PhD</fr:link> in verification strategies for financial <fr:link href="/dhsorens-000W/" title="Smart Contract Design, Specification, and Verification" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-000W/" display-uri="dhsorens-000W" type="local">smart contracts</fr:link>.

    Along the way, I became deeply interested in type theory and <fr:link href="/dhsorens-000B/" title="Interactive Theorem Provers" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-000B/" display-uri="dhsorens-000B" type="local">proof assistants</fr:link>, and these days am interested broadly in theorem-proving, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-notes/" title="Notes" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-notes/" display-uri="dhsorens-notes" type="local">whether applied to software or formalized maths</fr:link>.

    In my day-to-day, I still do a lot of work in the design, construction, and formal verification of smart contracts.
</html:p>
